From a09ce2c567d1179ddff58ea4dc8c8cb34c1a2d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evgeny Voropaev <evorop@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:16:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Finish legacy page conversion in an error-safe reading
 backend

AIO workers have no MultiXact visibility slot and shared completion cannot allocate or raise conversion errors safely. Publish pending conversion with BM_CONVERTED, then finish under the content lock before cached, forwarded, raced or waited read APIs expose the page. Reject pending recent-buffer pins so the normal API can handle them. Convert a validated private copy so ERROR leaves shared legacy data unchanged. Keep asynchronous physical I/O and deferred conversion images. Cross-version TAP passes 62 assertions against PG15.19, including wrapped MultiXacts, source epoch 1, repeated corrupt-header SQL errors, restart repair, standby recovery and CREATE DATABASE. Normalize wrapped target IDs only in xid32-source test comparisons.
